# SearXNG configuration — the search backend behind /v1/search.
#
# Copy to .env in this folder to configure `docker compose up` run FROM HERE. Running the
# root stack instead reads the repo-root .env, not this one — Compose only picks up the
# .env next to the file it was invoked with. Same variable names either way.
#
# Unlike the other services this is an upstream image, so these are SearXNG's own
# variable names rather than ours.

# Host port. Also used to build SEARXNG_BASE_URL, so changing it keeps the two in step.
# SEARXNG_PORT=8080

# Signs SearXNG's own tokens. The container entrypoint substitutes it into settings.yml
# at startup, replacing the placeholder there.
#
# The default is a known, committed development value — CHANGE IT before this instance is
# reachable by anyone but you:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
# SEARXNG_SECRET=

# --- Not set here ---
# SEARXNG_BASE_URL is derived from SEARXNG_PORT by docker-compose.yaml.
#
# The JSON API is the setting that actually matters, and it is NOT an environment
# variable: SearXNG ships it disabled and returns 403 without it. It is enabled by
# listing `json` under `search.formats` in settings.yml, which this folder mounts over
# the image's default. If /v1/search starts returning 403, check that the mount actually
# took effect — a path that fails to bind leaves the container writing its own default
# config, which looks identical to a config error.
#
# To point the backend at an instance you run elsewhere, set SEARXNG_URL on the BACKEND
# instead (see backend/.env.example) and do not start this service at all.
